# - Tables 6 and 7 evaluate each model on entire data sets, including its own training data, so a model's result on its own data set has role null and results on other data sets are external. For cross-validated data sets the paper also reports energy-difference RMSEs; the table values are encoded as given. The GAP-20 data set is matched to GAP-20U as its own set only by name (decision to confirm).
# - The NequIP MAEs on Owen-W (85.13 meV/atom, 69.02 meV/A) are quoted from Ref. 41 and not encoded. Sb and Te DFT settings are not described with the others; the functional is cited as GGA without being named. Elastic constants, defect and surface energies (Tables 2, 5) are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/subramanyam2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

